inal stream."] [139 1 "// FormatExceptionOnly is traceback.format_exception_only's text: a SyntaxError's location, source"] [140 1 "// line and caret, then \"Type: text\" (the type qualified by its module unless builtins), then the notes."] [145 23 "// traceback's stype: the module unless __main__ or builtins"] [149 3 "// str(exc) (traceback's _safe_string): a class's own __str__"] [229 1 "// RegisterSource gives sourceLine the text of a source that is no file (\"<stdin>\", \"<string>\"): the"] [230 1 "// REPL's statements, as linecache keeps them (PY5e's REQUEST, part 2a). A later text replaces it."] [235 1 "// sourceLine is the stripped text of line n of the file, \"\" when it does not read (linecache)."] [257 1 "// RunModule reads a module's IR (arbace.python.compile's code object as pr-str prints it) and runs it"] [258 1 "// as __main__ with file as __file__, on the process's stdout and stderr; the exit status: 0, 1 for an"] [259 1 "// uncaught exception (its traceback on stderr), SystemExit's code. bin/pyi run calls it."] [308 29 "// threading._shutdown: the non-daemon threads joined (Py_FinalizeEx, PY6f)"] [309 29 "// atexit's functions, as Py_FinalizeEx runs them (PY6a)"] [313 1 "// ExecModuleFile is ExecModule with __file__."] [333 44 "// an inlined comprehension's hidden locals"] [345 1 "// systemExitStatus is SystemExit's exit status: None 0, an int itself, else its str on stderr and 1."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[83 27] [94 28] [101 48] [104 43] [120 24] [120 35] [123 62] [131 37] [150 24] [170 47] [174 52] [177 56] [178 28] [182 56] [192 45] [203 24] [205 32] [273 18] [282 35] [285 52] [286 48] [297 28] [329 43] [350 36]]} (go/file "interp.go" :imports [


